 "capability": "crispr-guides",
 "title": "CRISPR guide assignment",
 "conclusion": "On 4 real screens (10x A549 and A375, Replogle 2022 K562, Norman 2019 K562), Singlet's guide calls agree with the published calls at the highest F1 on 4 of 4. They give 354.0 guides with a significant effect on their target, against 338.0 for the best other caller per screen. Where Singlet and Cell Ranger disagree on A549, the guides only Cell Ranger adds do not knock down their targets. 21 of 21 metrics pass.",
 "methods": "Guide UMIs are counted from the guide library's FASTQs by singlet.crispr (protospacer cut before the scaffold anchor, Cell Ranger feature-barcode logic for barcodes, guides and UMIs, 3' v3 barcode translation decided from the reads). Three callers run on the same counts and called cells: Singlet's ambient-calibrated test (the ambient profile from the library's empty droplets), a Cell Ranger-style per-guide GMM and a Poisson-Gaussian mixture. A549: Cell Ranger 6.0.0's published protospacer calls are the reference and a caller of their own. K562 (Replogle 2022, gem group 41): the authors' assignments; dual guides are compared as target genes; the protospacers were rebuilt from the sgRNA ids on hg19 (98% seen in reads). Knockdown: CP10k of each guide's target in its single-guide cells vs non-targeting cells (A549) or the cells of other targets (K562), one-sided Mann-Whitney, BH.",
 "status": "draft",
 "generated_at": "2026-10-26T16:25:31+00:00",
